  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/ca5e8035505f20619b6707d6d1f2d0b7b2f125a004a0dbd9d448840b0e4ffd99.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\sqrt{3}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\sqrt{3}}tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =tan\\,(\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\sqrt{3})-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
